From ed0d0f0968b34d5f82d9d4448cb0fbc5556c847e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:59:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] feat: performance profiles, a 30 Hz session cap and
 thread hints beyond the Odin 3

Seven profiles (Balanced, Performance, Battery saver, Compatibility, Xbox
PC games, Xbox Cloud, Steam) set existing settings together: the session
refresh cap, the FEX preset, the Steam client's cores (the efficiency
cluster on big.LITTLE CPUs), thread hints, shader pre-caching and
background downloads, and the Xbox Cloud stream. Changing any of them by
hand shows the profile as custom. Nothing touches clocks, thermal limits
or Android settings.

- The session refresh cap offers 30 Hz, an exact divisor of 60 Hz.
- Game thread performance hints can run on any SoC when a profile asks,
  and stop at THERMAL_STATUS_SEVERE there (CRITICAL on the Odin 3).
- Pinning the client can leave gamescope on every core.
- The web Xbox Cloud player picks the lowest display mode that shows its
  frame-rate limit, as the native player does.
- -PreleaseVersionNameSuffix names a release build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
